1017
00:32:32,968 --> 00:32:34,034
- [Rat Fink] Your distrust of me

1018
00:32:34,034 --> 00:32:36,334
 is grossly
 unjustified, Batwoman.

1019
00:32:36,334 --> 00:32:39,168
 However, I'll agree
 to your terms.

1020
00:32:40,401 --> 00:32:43,368
 12 o'clock on the top
 of Hangman's Bluff.

1021
00:32:43,368 --> 00:32:44,634
 - [Tom] Near Dead Man's Curve.

1022
00:32:44,634 --> 00:32:46,034
 - [Rat Fink] My men
 will meet you there.

1023
00:32:46,034 --> 00:32:47,401
- [Mike] You think they
get telemarketing calls

1024
00:32:47,401 --> 00:32:48,934
 on those wristwatches?

1025
00:32:48,934 --> 00:32:51,134
 Well, it looks like Rat Fink's
 doing all right for himself.

1026
00:32:51,134 --> 00:32:52,368
  (sobbing)

1027
00:32:52,368 --> 00:32:53,634
 - [Tom] Woah.

1028
00:32:53,634 --> 00:32:54,601
 - Give her another
 happy pill, will ya?

1029
00:32:54,601 --> 00:32:55,801
Can't stand it.

1030
00:32:57,168 --> 00:32:59,968
  - [Mike] She's had
  a breakthrough.

1031
00:33:01,668 --> 00:33:02,668
 - [Tom] Here, have a Mentos.

1032
00:33:02,668 --> 00:33:04,168
  Fresh goes better.

1033
00:33:05,701 --> 00:33:07,068
 (suspenseful orchestral music)

1034
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:08,534
 Dreezle drazzle drazzle drome.

1035
00:33:08,534 --> 00:33:11,468
 Time for this one to go home.

1036
00:33:11,468 --> 00:33:14,101
 - Just one of my many
 spectacular feats.

1037
00:33:14,101 --> 00:33:19,101
 I could make you so happy, you
 wouldn't believe it possible.

1038
00:33:19,834 --> 00:33:21,334
- Here.

1039
00:33:21,334 --> 00:33:22,901
 Why don't we all sit down and
 make ourselves comfortable?

1040
00:33:22,901 --> 00:33:25,001
I got some chocolate
milk in the refrigerator

1041
00:33:25,001 --> 00:33:26,568
 and some macaroons.

1042
00:33:26,568 --> 00:33:28,768
 Go ahead, sit down.

1043
00:33:28,768 --> 00:33:32,934
 - Well, I don't normally
 do this at meetings, but...

1044
00:33:32,934 --> 00:33:35,934
  - [Tom] Just park
  your bucket, Cher.

1045
00:33:37,001 --> 00:33:38,201
 She's got a frontal bike rack.

1046
00:33:38,201 --> 00:33:39,034
 Woah.

1047
00:33:40,801 --> 00:33:42,534
(growls)

1048
00:33:42,534 --> 00:33:44,068
  - [Mike] Criminy.

1049
00:33:44,068 --> 00:33:46,934
  It's like a Warhol movie,
  except it's kind of weird.

1050
00:33:46,934 --> 00:33:51,201
 - [Tom] Chaka Khan would be
 ashamed to dress like her.

1051
00:33:51,201 --> 00:33:52,401
  - Uh, none for me, thanks.

1052
00:33:52,401 --> 00:33:54,468
I'm lactose intolerant.

1053
00:33:54,468 --> 00:33:56,201
  - How long am I to
  be kept waiting?

1054
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:58,101
 - Oh, not for long, I'm sure.

1055
00:33:58,101 --> 00:33:59,068
 - [Tom] Hey.

1056
00:33:59,068 --> 00:34:00,434
- At any moment, I expect that--

1057
00:34:00,434 --> 00:34:01,868
 (cyberphone beeping)
 (laughs)

1058
00:34:01,868 --> 00:34:03,101
 There you are.

1059
00:34:03,101 --> 00:34:05,034
  You see, no sooner
  said than done.

1060
00:34:05,034 --> 00:34:06,734
  Oh, you can call--

1061
00:34:06,734 --> 00:34:08,368
 - [Mike] Kind of an
 odd Thanksgiving,

1062
00:34:08,368 --> 00:34:09,734
  but the sentiment's there.

1063
00:34:09,734 --> 00:34:10,701
  - [Tom] Oh, yeah.

1064
00:34:10,701 --> 00:34:13,268
 (upbeat music)

1065
00:34:18,001 --> 00:34:21,001
 (chuckles)
 (cyberphone beeping)

1066
00:34:21,001 --> 00:34:22,934
 - [Tom] I turned
 the switch on, boss.

1067
00:34:22,934 --> 00:34:24,634
 - Well, my adversary.

1068
00:34:24,634 --> 00:34:25,901
  So we meet again.

1069
00:34:25,901 --> 00:34:27,134
 - [Mike] Him again.

1070
00:34:27,134 --> 00:34:29,268
- [Rat Fink] Welcome to
my humble facilities.

1071
00:34:29,268 --> 00:34:30,534
 - So we meet again.

1072
00:34:30,534 --> 00:34:31,768
 But for the first
 time on your terms.

1073
00:34:31,768 --> 00:34:33,168
 - [Mike] Have some Rolaids.

1074
00:34:33,168 --> 00:34:34,668
Calcium.

1075
00:34:34,668 --> 00:34:36,268
 - I can't recall ever being
 placed in a position where

1076
00:34:36,268 --> 00:34:39,634
  I would perpetuate
  your evil plans.

1077
00:34:39,634 --> 00:34:41,701
  - Now you might think
  that the iocane powder is

1078
00:34:41,701 --> 00:34:42,901
 in this one.

1079
00:34:42,901 --> 00:34:44,368
- There are great things
we can do together,

1080
00:34:44,368 --> 00:34:46,568
 things that could bring
 unheard of power and riches

1081
00:34:46,568 --> 00:34:47,834
 to both of us.

1082
00:34:47,834 --> 00:34:49,934
 - [Tom] Is she doing a
 rain dance back there?

1083
00:34:49,934 --> 00:34:51,434
 - I'm only here
 because I have to be,

1084
00:34:51,434 --> 00:34:53,834
 and it won't be for
 much longer at that.

1085
00:34:53,834 --> 00:34:55,268
Get on with your dirty business.

1086
00:34:55,268 --> 00:34:57,134
 - [Mike] She brings a
 quiet dignity to this film.

1087
00:34:57,134 --> 00:34:58,368
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

1088
00:34:58,368 --> 00:34:59,968
 - As I've mentioned
 previously, I want

1089
00:34:59,968 --> 00:35:02,168
 you to get something
 for me that I

1090
00:35:02,168 --> 00:35:04,468
  wanted personally
  for a long time.

1091
00:35:04,468 --> 00:35:06,301
  - Mittens.

1092
00:35:06,301 --> 00:35:08,501
  - [Rat Fink] The
  Ayjax Development
  Corporation has developed

1093
00:35:08,501 --> 00:35:10,234
an atomic hearing aid--

1094
00:35:10,234 --> 00:35:13,234
- [Tom] We'll destroy
Miracle-Ear and rule the world!

1095
00:35:13,234 --> 00:35:16,501
 - Any telephone
 conversation desired.

1096
00:35:16,501 --> 00:35:18,168
  Since it has this
  potential, the government

1097
00:35:18,168 --> 00:35:19,334
has refused the patent.

1098
00:35:19,334 --> 00:35:21,068
- [Mike] I, I, I, I, I.

1099
00:35:21,068 --> 00:35:23,301
  (mumbling)

1100
00:35:24,668 --> 00:35:25,501
  (groaning)

1101
00:35:25,501 --> 00:35:26,434
  - [Tom] Sieg Heil.

1102
00:35:26,434 --> 00:35:27,734
- [Rat Fink] An assignment such

1103
00:35:27,734 --> 00:35:29,568
as this would be entirely within

1104
00:35:29,568 --> 00:35:32,901
 the realm of your own
 many splendid talents.

1105
00:35:32,901 --> 00:35:34,134
  - [Mike] What can you say?

1106
00:35:34,134 --> 00:35:36,068
 It's a tour de force
 comic performance.

1107
00:35:36,068 --> 00:35:37,534
  - Every--

1108
00:35:37,534 --> 00:35:39,068
  - [Rat Fink] Neon,
  you idiotic fool!

1109
00:35:39,068 --> 00:35:40,234
What do you think you're doing?

1110
00:35:40,234 --> 00:35:41,668
 - [Tom] I got the music in me.

1111
00:35:41,668 --> 00:35:43,534
 - I must have switched
 the, the glasses, Batwoman.

1112
00:35:43,534 --> 00:35:47,868
 I, I only wanted to show
 you how wonderful they are.

1113
00:35:48,768 --> 00:35:50,734
I could make you happy.

1114
00:35:50,734 --> 00:35:52,701
  - Oh, his parents
  must be so proud.

1115
00:35:52,701 --> 00:35:55,001
  (babbling)

1116
00:35:55,001 --> 00:35:57,301
 - [Mike] Hey,
 you're a guest here.

1117
00:35:57,301 --> 00:35:58,134
 Ouch.

1118
00:35:59,268 --> 00:36:00,968
 (upbeat rock music)

1119
00:36:00,968 --> 00:36:02,234
  - [Tom] Where's
  that coming from?

1120
00:36:02,234 --> 00:36:03,401
- Well, we've discovered
Batwoman's secret power.

1121
00:36:03,401 --> 00:36:05,768
 She can open unlocked doors.

1122
00:36:05,768 --> 00:36:09,234
 - [Tom] So this is the wild,
 wild world of Batwoman, eh?

1123
00:36:09,234 --> 00:36:10,401
 Hmm?

1124
00:36:10,401 --> 00:36:11,934
 - [Mike] What happa?

1125
00:36:11,934 --> 00:36:13,201
 - [Tom] Ohh.

1126
00:36:13,201 --> 00:36:14,534
- [Tom] Yes, it's the best hits

1127
00:36:14,534 --> 00:36:18,368
of the '50s and '60s on
8-track and cassettes.

1128
00:36:19,401 --> 00:36:21,268
- [All] Tequila.

1129
00:36:21,268 --> 00:36:22,934
 - [Mike] Yeah.

1130
00:36:22,934 --> 00:36:25,701
 - Those two were once
 cute, tiny, lovable babies.

1131
00:36:25,701 --> 00:36:27,201
 - [Mike] Tequil, oh.

1132
00:36:27,201 --> 00:36:30,168
- [Tom] Meanwhile well in Rome.

1133
00:36:30,168 --> 00:36:32,468
- [All] Aye-ja- Aye-jax?

1134
00:36:32,468 --> 00:36:33,801
Aye-jax.

1135
00:36:33,801 --> 00:36:34,634
  Ai-yi-yi,

1136
00:36:34,634 --> 00:36:35,468
 Aie.

1137
00:36:37,434 --> 00:36:38,301
  - We're in trouble

1138
00:36:38,301 --> 00:36:39,768
 - [Tom] Hmm?

1139
00:36:39,768 --> 00:36:40,568
 - [Mike] I have no idea what
 I'm doing in this movie.

1140
00:36:40,568 --> 00:36:41,868
 - Deep, deep trouble.

1141
00:36:41,868 --> 00:36:43,434
- Oh, take it easy, JB.

1142
00:36:43,434 --> 00:36:44,968
 We don't have to
 throw in the sponge

1143
00:36:44,968 --> 00:36:46,901
 just because we're
 hanging on the ropes.

1144
00:36:46,901 --> 00:36:47,968
 - [Tom] Hmm?

1145
00:36:47,968 --> 00:36:49,601
 - That's an understatement.

1146
00:36:49,601 --> 00:36:51,968
  I'd say it was more like
  being pulled to the corner

1147
00:36:51,968 --> 00:36:53,068
  after a nine cone.

1148
00:36:53,068 --> 00:36:54,001
  (chuckles)

1149
00:36:54,001 --> 00:36:55,501
 - Oh, Larry Tate, that's rich.

1150
00:36:55,501 --> 00:36:58,101
 - Now, look, I have the legal
 department working overtime.

1151
00:36:58,101 --> 00:36:59,601
- [Tom] And she's really tired.

1152
00:36:59,601 --> 00:37:01,034
 - We've got plenty of time to
 come up with something, JB.

1153
00:37:01,034 --> 00:37:02,801
  - Look, Flanagan--

1154
00:37:02,801 --> 00:37:04,034
 - [Mike] That's me.

1155
00:37:04,034 --> 00:37:05,701
 - There's been some
 speculation in my mind

1156
00:37:05,701 --> 00:37:07,034
 about talking to you.

1157
00:37:07,034 --> 00:37:07,901
 - Oh, really?

1158
00:37:07,901 --> 00:37:08,834
 - [Mike] That's good.

1159
00:37:08,834 --> 00:37:10,068
  You weren't in the office.

1160
00:37:10,068 --> 00:37:11,501
 - I'm afraid there
 exists a few aspects

1161
00:37:11,501 --> 00:37:15,534
to this business about our
patent being denied that, well,

1162
00:37:15,534 --> 00:37:17,434
 that I haven't brought
 out fully before.

1163
00:37:17,434 --> 00:37:18,868
 - And you're
 sitting on my lunch.

1164
00:37:18,868 --> 00:37:22,201
 - A few weeks ago I was
 contacted by a foreign agent.

1165
00:37:22,201 --> 00:37:23,134
 - [Tom] This just in.

1166
00:37:23,134 --> 00:37:24,368
  - A foreign agent?

1167
00:37:24,368 --> 00:37:26,068
 You didn't make a deal
 with them, did you?

1168
00:37:26,068 --> 00:37:27,201
 - Well, of course I didn't.

1169
00:37:27,201 --> 00:37:28,134
 - [Mike] I'm sorry.

1170
00:37:28,134 --> 00:37:29,368
  I didn't mean to lash out.

1171
00:37:29,368 --> 00:37:30,601
  - Stories carried
  by his cronies,

1172
00:37:30,601 --> 00:37:32,301
 I'm sure a few people
 assumed that I did.

1173
00:37:32,301 --> 00:37:35,134
 Oh, look, Flanagan,
 I realize you've

1174
00:37:35,134 --> 00:37:37,701
  got our legal boys
  trying to concoct

1175
00:37:37,701 --> 00:37:40,001
 some sort of appeal for us.

1176
00:37:40,001 --> 00:37:41,268
 But the terrible thing is--

1177
00:37:41,268 --> 00:37:42,534
  - [Tom] You're on
  my tuna sandwich.

1178
00:37:42,534 --> 00:37:44,934
- I never told you this either.

1179
00:37:44,934 --> 00:37:48,068
 Our time limit for destroying
 that device has run out.

1180
00:37:48,068 --> 00:37:49,201
 - [Tom] What device?

1181
00:37:49,201 --> 00:37:50,668
 Who are you?

1182
00:37:50,668 --> 00:37:54,234
  - We had just 15 days,
  not 30 as I told everyone.

1183
00:37:54,234 --> 00:37:56,601
 - JB, you kept that
 thing here illegally.

1184
00:37:56,601 --> 00:37:57,868
  - [Tom] You dope.

1185
00:37:57,868 --> 00:37:59,168
 - Hoping we wouldn't
 have to destroy it?

1186
00:37:59,168 --> 00:38:01,368
 - Well, get ready for
 the worst part of all.

1187
00:38:01,368 --> 00:38:03,301
- [Mike] I've hired
Willie Tyler and Lester.

1188
00:38:03,301 --> 00:38:04,501
 - I received a telephone call

1189
00:38:04,501 --> 00:38:06,601
  early this morning
  from Batwoman.

1190
00:38:06,601 --> 00:38:08,068
 - [Tom] Hmm?

1191
00:38:08,068 --> 00:38:09,868
 - She was good enough to
 inform me to be on the alert

1192
00:38:09,868 --> 00:38:11,868
  that extensive
  planning was being

1193
00:38:11,868 --> 00:38:14,201
executed for an attempted theft.

1194
00:38:14,201 --> 00:38:15,668
  - Does she know
  that to be a fact?

1195
00:38:15,668 --> 00:38:19,168
 - If she didn't, she
 wouldn't have called.

1196
00:38:19,168 --> 00:38:21,201
  - [Tom] I have no clue
  what you're talking about,

1197
00:38:21,201 --> 00:38:24,434
 but I'm profoundly devastated.

1198
00:38:24,434 --> 00:38:26,201
(gasps)

1199
00:38:26,201 --> 00:38:31,201
- Well, now that you've informed
me of our legal position,

1200
00:38:32,334 --> 00:38:33,268
 I suppose asking
 the police for help

1201
00:38:33,268 --> 00:38:34,934
 is highly questionable, JB.

1202
00:38:34,934 --> 00:38:36,201
  - [Tom] I oughta--

1203
00:38:36,201 --> 00:38:38,768
 - Why didn't you tell
 me about this sooner?

1204
00:38:38,768 --> 00:38:41,201
What do you think I'm here for?

1205
00:38:41,201 --> 00:38:42,268
  - I want you to spank me.

1206
00:38:42,268 --> 00:38:43,534
- I was afraid.

1207
00:38:44,734 --> 00:38:46,568
 And I was hoping for
 some kind of appeal

1208
00:38:46,568 --> 00:38:47,834
 to the patent office.

1209
00:38:47,834 --> 00:38:49,201
 - [Mike] And I didn't
 steal no bike neither.

1210
00:38:49,201 --> 00:38:50,568
 - Well, we've just gotta think

1211
00:38:50,568 --> 00:38:52,268
 of something to tighten it up.

1212
00:38:52,268 --> 00:38:53,734
 That's all.

1213
00:38:53,734 --> 00:38:55,201
 - You just don't care about
 my lunch at all, do you?

1214
00:38:55,201 --> 00:38:56,634
 You know it's there, and
 you deliberately sit on it.

1215
00:38:56,634 --> 00:38:57,901
- Wait a minute.

1216
00:38:57,901 --> 00:38:58,701
 - We're not supposed
 to be in this movie.

1217
00:38:58,701 --> 00:39:00,268
 - Wait a minute, JB.

1218
00:39:00,268 --> 00:39:01,768
 I think I've got it.

1219
00:39:01,768 --> 00:39:02,968
 - [Mike] The rain in Spain
 falls mainly on the plains.

1220
00:39:02,968 --> 00:39:03,934
 - Batwoman.

1221
00:39:03,934 --> 00:39:05,201
  (gasps)
  (chuckles)

1222
00:39:05,201 --> 00:39:08,034
 - With her, we might
 see some light yet.

1223
00:39:08,034 --> 00:39:09,234
 (upbeat jazz music)

1224
00:39:09,234 --> 00:39:10,168
 - [Mike] It's over.

1225
00:39:10,168 --> 00:39:12,301
 (clapping)
 (all groaning)

1226
00:39:12,301 --> 00:39:15,634
 Now this shot here,
 this is pure Warren.

1227
00:39:17,268 --> 00:39:18,434
 - [Tom] Thursday afternoon,

1228
00:39:18,434 --> 00:39:20,001
 I pulled up at this one place.

1229
00:39:20,001 --> 00:39:22,834
 I don't know what time it was.

1230
00:39:22,834 --> 00:39:25,168
 I kind of got out of my car.

1231
00:39:26,034 --> 00:39:28,301
 I looked at the place.

1232
00:39:28,301 --> 00:39:30,001
 I walked towards some
 sort of structure

1233
00:39:30,001 --> 00:39:33,401
  in which people
  possibly dwelled.

1234
00:39:33,401 --> 00:39:35,568
  I noticed the agriculture.

1235
00:39:37,101 --> 00:39:39,634
 The sound editor added
 a tasty sax lick.

1236
00:39:39,634 --> 00:39:42,701
 I passed a tree or a
 shrub of some variety.

1237
00:39:42,701 --> 00:39:44,268
 Then I arrived at the door.

1238
00:39:44,268 --> 00:39:45,401
 (mysterious orchestral music)

1239
00:39:45,401 --> 00:39:46,634
 Ooh.

1240
00:39:46,634 --> 00:39:50,134
I went through the door,
and it was quite cool.

1241
00:39:51,534 --> 00:39:53,368
 I had heard Batwoman had
 quite a lingerie collection.

1242
00:39:53,368 --> 00:39:55,468
  I decided to investigate.

1243
00:39:57,468 --> 00:39:58,768
 (light organ music)

1244
00:39:58,768 --> 00:39:59,601
 Hmm?

1245
00:40:00,801 --> 00:40:01,968
 - [Mike] D'oh!

1246
00:40:01,968 --> 00:40:03,001
 The one day they
 aren't wearing bikinis

1247
00:40:03,001 --> 00:40:04,434
is the day I stopped by.

1248
00:40:04,434 --> 00:40:07,034
(groans)

1249
00:40:07,034 --> 00:40:07,868
 - Oh, good.

1250
00:40:07,868 --> 00:40:09,768
Here's the receptionist.

1251
00:40:09,768 --> 00:40:13,234
- [Tom] Are you with
the bride or the groom?

1252
00:40:13,234 --> 00:40:14,501
- I'm with you.

1253
00:40:15,634 --> 00:40:17,168
 Hey, weren't you
 in "Beast Master 2,

1254
00:40:17,168 --> 00:40:19,568
 "Through the Portal of Time"?

1255
00:40:21,001 --> 00:40:22,934
 - [Tom] Toccata
 and wow in D minor.

1256
00:40:22,934 --> 00:40:23,768
(purrs)

1257
00:40:23,768 --> 00:40:24,701
 - You know it.

1258
00:40:24,701 --> 00:40:25,834
 Oh, she's jamming right now.

1259
00:40:25,834 --> 00:40:27,601
 She might be a while.

1260
00:40:31,434 --> 00:40:33,568
 - [Mike] After six months of
 lessons from Schmitt Music,

1261
00:40:33,568 --> 00:40:35,834
 I'm playing for my friends.

1262
00:40:39,601 --> 00:40:40,568
  - [Tom] Mm, sorry.

1263
00:40:40,568 --> 00:40:42,701
  This is a smoke-free cult.

1264
00:40:48,801 --> 00:40:49,734
 You know, for a movie.

1265
00:40:49,734 --> 00:40:51,934
  (chuckles)

1266
00:40:53,434 --> 00:40:57,268
  - [Mike] That was Michael
  Murry on "Pipedreams."

1267
00:40:57,268 --> 00:40:58,401
  - I wonder if it's
  hard to sight-read

1268
00:40:58,401 --> 00:40:59,301
 through those glasses.

1269
00:40:59,301 --> 00:41:00,168
 - [Tom] I bet.

1270
00:41:00,168 --> 00:41:00,934
 - Batwoman.

1271
00:41:00,934 --> 00:41:01,934
 - [Mike] Hi.

1272
00:41:03,101 --> 00:41:05,268
  - Oh, uh, about that door,

1273
00:41:06,401 --> 00:41:07,901
 that's a little
 dangerous, isn't it?

1274
00:41:07,901 --> 00:41:09,601
 - [Tom] He's really going to
 stick to that vinyl, you know.

1275
00:41:09,601 --> 00:41:11,068
  - It wouldn't have
  operated if you

1276
00:41:11,068 --> 00:41:13,801
  had no appointment or
  someone was following you.

1277
00:41:13,801 --> 00:41:15,301
  You were monitored
  electronically

1278
00:41:15,301 --> 00:41:16,868
from the time you left your car.

1279
00:41:16,868 --> 00:41:18,034
 - Oh, really?

1280
00:41:18,034 --> 00:41:19,501
 - [Tom] Yeah, right.

1281
00:41:19,501 --> 00:41:21,668
  - Oh, you mean like a
  closed circuit television.

1282
00:41:21,668 --> 00:41:23,368
 - Something like that.

1283
00:41:23,368 --> 00:41:25,701
 - [Mike] Jell-O shot, ma'am?

1284
00:41:27,634 --> 00:41:28,868
 - [Tom] Hmm?

1285
00:41:28,868 --> 00:41:29,668
  - Would you like
  some refreshments?

1286
00:41:29,668 --> 00:41:30,634
- Uh, no, no, thank you.

1287
00:41:30,634 --> 00:41:32,134
  I'm fine.

1288
00:41:32,134 --> 00:41:34,868
  Uh, very nice of you to
  see me this way, Batwoman.

1289
00:41:34,868 --> 00:41:37,034
  And I want you to know
  that JB and the rest of us

1290
00:41:37,034 --> 00:41:39,201
(glugging)
will be forever grateful

1291
00:41:39,201 --> 00:41:42,134
if, well, if you can just
figure out some way to help us.

1292
00:41:42,134 --> 00:41:43,768
 (all shouting)

1293
00:41:43,768 --> 00:41:44,734
 - [Mike] I hate those.

1294
00:41:44,734 --> 00:41:45,701
 - Someone who would listen in

1295
00:41:45,701 --> 00:41:47,001
to someone else's conversations.

1296
00:41:47,001 --> 00:41:49,434
- Oh, Batwoman, you
really don't think that,

1297
00:41:49,434 --> 00:41:50,834
 that JB and I would--

1298
00:41:50,834 --> 00:41:51,734
 - Jim Beam?

1299
00:41:51,734 --> 00:41:52,701
  (chuckles)

1300
00:41:52,701 --> 00:41:54,268
  - [Mike] Justice Brothers.

1301
00:41:54,268 --> 00:41:55,901
 - Oh, I'm not interested in
 anyone else's conversation.

1302
00:41:55,901 --> 00:41:57,134
No, no.

1303
00:41:57,134 --> 00:41:58,734
 You have the wrong
 idea, entirely wrong.

1304
00:41:58,734 --> 00:42:00,601
 - [Tom] Is this supposed
 to be an all-staff meeting?

1305
00:42:00,601 --> 00:42:02,668
  - As a matter of fact,
  the atomic power structure

1306
00:42:02,668 --> 00:42:06,234
was much more revolutionary
than anything we had counted on.

1307
00:42:06,234 --> 00:42:07,434
 - [Mike] Hey.

1308
00:42:07,434 --> 00:42:08,934
 You'd think just
 being Batwoman she'd

1309
00:42:08,934 --> 00:42:11,001
 have more exciting meetings,
 but this is just painful.

1310
00:42:11,001 --> 00:42:12,901
- Goes, it really goes.

1311
00:42:12,901 --> 00:42:14,968
 But the main thing
 is if we could just--

1312
00:42:14,968 --> 00:42:16,201
  - [Tom] Now what?

1313
00:42:16,201 --> 00:42:17,601
 - Hang onto it until
 our appeal is okayed--

1314
00:42:17,601 --> 00:42:19,968
- So there's a subplot
about a horseshoe then.

1315
00:42:19,968 --> 00:42:21,001
 - [Tom] I guess so.

1316
00:42:21,001 --> 00:42:22,368
- A little bit more development,

1317
00:42:22,368 --> 00:42:23,968
 we can make a great
 contribution to, uh, society.

1318
00:42:23,968 --> 00:42:25,034
 - [Mike] Will you--

1319
00:42:25,034 --> 00:42:26,168
 - [Tom] Gimme.

1320
00:42:26,168 --> 00:42:27,034
 - But the big problem
 is, Batwoman--

1321
00:42:27,034 --> 00:42:27,968
- [Tom] Let me have it.

1322
00:42:27,968 --> 00:42:30,101
 - If it's stolen, we're sunk.

1323
00:42:30,101 --> 00:42:32,601
  If our device is
  misused, Batwoman,

1324
00:42:32,601 --> 00:42:34,234
there's no telling what
can be accomplished.

1325
00:42:34,234 --> 00:42:35,468
  (grunting)

1326
00:42:35,468 --> 00:42:36,701
  - [Mike] You have
  beautiful eyes.

1327
00:42:36,701 --> 00:42:38,134
 - Do you realize there
 will be no privacy?

1328
00:42:38,134 --> 00:42:41,134
And just consider the
danger if they find out

1329
00:42:41,134 --> 00:42:42,234
 about the cobalt mechanism.

1330
00:42:42,234 --> 00:42:43,168
- [Tom] Stop it.

1331
00:42:43,168 --> 00:42:44,268
 Would you stop it back there?

1332
00:42:44,268 --> 00:42:45,201
  - I can see it's--

1333
00:42:45,201 --> 00:42:46,201
 - [Mike] Let's get outta here.

1334
00:42:46,201 --> 00:42:47,134
 - Avoided at any cost.

1335
00:42:47,134 --> 00:42:48,601
  - Oh, good, you'll do it.

1336
00:42:48,601 --> 00:42:50,501
You'll come in with us.

1337
00:42:51,968 --> 00:42:53,934
 - Give me some time
 to talk with my girls.

1338
00:42:53,934 --> 00:42:55,334
 I'll call you within the hour.

1339
00:42:55,334 --> 00:42:56,401
 - Fine, fine.

1340
00:42:57,768 --> 00:43:00,368
 (upbeat music)

1341
00:43:03,901 --> 00:43:07,301
 - And in preparing my report
 on today's cheating short,

1342
00:43:07,301 --> 00:43:09,734
 I listened to both
 the muse and the sage,

1343
00:43:09,734 --> 00:43:12,468
the spirit and the
pragmatist, the mythical

1344
00:43:12,468 --> 00:43:13,801
 roots of my eternal--

1345
00:43:13,801 --> 00:43:15,901
 - Oh, any time this
 century, Disraeli.

1346
00:43:15,901 --> 00:43:17,168
- Crow, come on.

1347
00:43:17,168 --> 00:43:20,034
- Oh, okay, Mike, just
wake me when it's over.

1348
00:43:20,034 --> 00:43:22,701
  - Anyway, as I was saying,
  it was the third question

1349
00:43:22,701 --> 00:43:24,168
that most intrigued me.

1350
00:43:24,168 --> 00:43:26,968
 The query, was it fair for
 Johnny to use Mary as he did,

1351
00:43:26,968 --> 00:43:28,434
 is a mental minefield.

1352
00:43:28,434 --> 00:43:30,768
  I had to be careful, being
  the humist that I am.

1353
00:43:30,768 --> 00:43:32,034
  I left no stone unturned.

1354
00:43:32,034 --> 00:43:33,334
  - Any time, Servo.

1355
00:43:33,334 --> 00:43:34,601
  Any time.

1356
00:43:34,601 --> 00:43:38,101
  - Uh, that answer,
  my friends, is no.

1357
00:43:38,101 --> 00:43:38,934
  Thank you.

1358
00:43:38,934 --> 00:43:39,768
 - No?

1359
00:43:39,768 --> 00:43:40,634
- That's right.

1360
00:43:40,634 --> 00:43:42,368
 Nyet, nein, negigey.

1361
00:43:42,368 --> 00:43:44,268
 - That's your report,
 the answer is no?

1362
00:43:44,268 --> 00:43:45,668
 What about all
 these other volumes?

1363
00:43:45,668 --> 00:43:47,501
 - Well, jeez, Mike,
 I had several ibids,

1364
00:43:47,501 --> 00:43:48,968
 30 pages of footnotes,

1365
00:43:48,968 --> 00:43:51,434
 an extensive bibliography,
 and some really neat diagrams

1366
00:43:51,434 --> 00:43:53,368
 charting the dielectric
 process from the Freudian--

1367
00:43:53,368 --> 00:43:56,001
- You know, Tom,
you frighten me.

1368
00:43:56,001 --> 00:43:56,868
 So we're done, huh?

1369
00:43:56,868 --> 00:43:58,268
 - No, we're not done.

1370
00:43:58,268 --> 00:43:59,534
 We've still got Gypsy.

1371
00:43:59,534 --> 00:44:00,768
  Why don't you go
  ahead there, girl?

1372
00:44:00,768 --> 00:44:01,601
- Yeah.

1373
00:44:01,601 --> 00:44:03,501
 - Um, oh, oh, okay.

1374
00:44:03,501 --> 00:44:04,601
 Um, cheating.

1375
00:44:06,301 --> 00:44:07,134
 By me.

1376
00:44:07,134 --> 00:44:07,968
 - Hm.

1377
00:44:07,968 --> 00:44:09,801
  - Cheating is bad.

1378
00:44:09,801 --> 00:44:11,968
  Richard Baseheart is good.

1379
00:44:12,901 --> 00:44:13,734
 Well?

1380
00:44:13,734 --> 00:44:14,568
 - Huh.

1381
00:44:14,568 --> 00:44:15,734
 Great.

1382
00:44:15,734 --> 00:44:16,534
 - Well, that was
 very good, I thought.

1383
00:44:16,534 --> 00:44:17,501
  - Yeah, very nice.

1384
00:44:17,501 --> 00:44:19,068
 - It was spirited, succinct.

1385
00:44:19,068 --> 00:44:19,901
  Very nice.

1386
00:44:19,901 --> 00:44:20,734
 - Right to the point.

1387
00:44:20,734 --> 00:44:21,934
- Great.

1388
00:44:21,934 --> 00:44:22,868
 - Can't we just
 hand these in, Mike?

1389
00:44:22,868 --> 00:44:23,668
  I mean, notify me by mail.

1390
00:44:23,668 --> 00:44:24,368
  - No, no, no, no.

1391
00:44:24,368 --> 00:44:25,201
It's your turn.

1392
00:44:25,201 --> 00:44:26,034
  Now let's hear it.

1393
00:44:26,034 --> 00:44:26,868
Come on.

1394
00:44:26,868 --> 00:44:28,034
 - Oh.

1395
00:44:28,034 --> 00:44:28,868
  Cheating.

1396
00:44:28,868 --> 00:44:30,468
(clears throat)

1397
00:44:30,468 --> 00:44:31,801
Cheating is bad.

1398
00:44:34,034 --> 00:44:36,968
  Richard Baseheart is good.

1399
00:44:36,968 --> 00:44:37,901
 - Ooh.

1400
00:44:37,901 --> 00:44:38,634
  - So how about some lunch?

1401
00:44:38,634 --> 00:44:39,468
 - Hey, Crow.

1402
00:44:39,468 --> 00:44:40,601
- What?

1403
00:44:40,601 --> 00:44:41,434
- That was word-for-word
the same report

1404
00:44:41,434 --> 00:44:42,701
 that Gypsy just gave.

1405
00:44:42,701 --> 00:44:43,534
 (chuckles nervously)

1406
00:44:43,534 --> 00:44:44,801
 - Wow.

1407
00:44:44,801 --> 00:44:46,034
  What are the odds
  of that happening?

1408
00:44:46,034 --> 00:44:47,234
  - It's, it's not
  exactly the same.

1409
00:44:47,234 --> 00:44:48,501
 I, I mean the read
 was totally different.

1410
00:44:48,501 --> 00:44:50,134
 Uh, my downbeat was on good.

1411
00:44:50,134 --> 00:44:51,534
 Uh, Gypsy's was on Richard.

1412
00:44:51,534 --> 00:44:53,101
- Scold him, scold him.

1413
00:44:53,101 --> 00:44:54,201
  Cheater, cheater!

1414
00:44:54,201 --> 00:44:55,134
 - Hey, hey, hey, hey.

1415
00:44:55,134 --> 00:44:55,968
  Calm down.

1416
00:44:55,968 --> 00:44:57,234
  Calm down.

1417
00:44:57,234 --> 00:44:58,034
  You know, this is
  serious business,

1418
00:44:58,034 --> 00:44:59,301
and we'll talk about it.

1419
00:44:59,301 --> 00:45:00,601
But right now we've got
a movie to get through,

1420
00:45:00,601 --> 00:45:01,768
  and that's what
  we're going to do.

1421
00:45:01,768 --> 00:45:03,268
 - We, we must demolate him.

1422
00:45:03,268 --> 00:45:04,101
 Get a match.

1423
00:45:04,101 --> 00:45:04,934
  Burn him.

1424
00:45:04,934 --> 00:45:05,768
(alarm buzzing)

1425
00:45:05,768 --> 00:45:06,601
 - Ah.

1426
00:45:06,601 --> 00:45:07,434
 Movie time.

1427
00:45:07,434 --> 00:45:08,268
  Saved by the bell.

1428
00:45:08,268 --> 00:45:09,168
 - Burn him!

1429
00:45:18,901 --> 00:45:20,101
Burn, I'm sorry.

1430
00:45:20,101 --> 00:45:21,001
  I'm sorry.

1431
00:45:21,001 --> 00:45:21,834
I just lost it.

1432
00:45:21,834 --> 00:45:22,734
 - Up close.

1433
00:45:24,068 --> 00:45:25,101
Come on.

1434
00:45:25,101 --> 00:45:25,934
 - [Mike] Huh?

1435
00:45:25,934 --> 00:45:26,768
  (chuckles)

1436
00:45:26,768 --> 00:45:27,934
 - Right here.

1437
00:45:27,934 --> 00:45:29,168
 - [Tom] Little
 piggy, little piggy.

1438
00:45:29,168 --> 00:45:30,901
 - [Mike] Heathcliff
 shops at Tatters.

1439
00:45:30,901 --> 00:45:33,134
 - I have something for you.

1440
00:45:34,234 --> 00:45:35,268
  (chuckles)

1441
00:45:35,268 --> 00:45:37,034
 Now open your mouth.

1442
00:45:37,034 --> 00:45:39,301
- I hope that's cyanide.

1443
00:45:39,301 --> 00:45:42,001
  - Oh, Heathcliff, this
  is not going to hurt you.

1444
00:45:42,001 --> 00:45:43,201
- [Mike] It's going to kill you.

1445
00:45:43,201 --> 00:45:44,501
  - I just perfected
  a new formula,

1446
00:45:44,501 --> 00:45:46,901
 and I must test its reaction.

1447
00:45:48,334 --> 00:45:51,468
 Whatever it does, it will
 only last for a short time.

1448
00:45:51,468 --> 00:45:53,334
- [Tom] And it will
pad the film immensely.

1449
00:45:53,334 --> 00:45:54,768
 - Oh, come on.

1450
00:45:54,768 --> 00:45:56,101
Open your mouth.

1451
00:45:57,501 --> 00:45:59,601
  Oh, Heathcliff, I'm losing
  my patience with you.

1452
00:45:59,601 --> 00:46:00,901
- Yeah.

1453
00:46:00,901 --> 00:46:01,701
  I bet he's lost a
  lot of patients.

1454
00:46:01,701 --> 00:46:02,901
 - [Mike] Oh, shut up.

1455
00:46:02,901 --> 00:46:05,668
 - I'll tell you,
 I'll tell you what.

1456
00:46:05,668 --> 00:46:07,601
If you take this pill--

1457
00:46:07,601 --> 00:46:09,301
 - [Tom] I will stop
 talking like Gandhi.

1458
00:46:09,301 --> 00:46:14,301
- When I go to that underground
cave, I'll take you with me,

1459
00:46:15,434 --> 00:46:18,268
 and you'll be able
 to see some monsters.

1460
00:46:18,268 --> 00:46:22,668
You can watch them all the time
that I am in the big cavern.

1461
00:46:22,668 --> 00:46:24,468
- Because I'm vaguely European.

1462
00:46:24,468 --> 00:46:26,001
  - Wouldn't you like that?

1463
00:46:26,001 --> 00:46:26,834
 Hmm?

1464
00:46:26,834 --> 00:46:27,668
 Huh?

1465
00:46:27,668 --> 00:46:29,534
 (Mike sighs)

1466
00:46:29,534 --> 00:46:30,968
 - [Mike] Ohh.

1467
00:46:30,968 --> 00:46:32,534
  Trying to be both a
  mother and a father to you

1468
00:46:32,534 --> 00:46:34,368
is so difficult.

1469
00:46:34,368 --> 00:46:36,234
(buzzer ringing)

1470
00:46:36,234 --> 00:46:37,268
  - [Tom] Could this
  please be the end

1471
00:46:37,268 --> 00:46:38,368
  of the pill-taking scene?

1472
00:46:38,368 --> 00:46:39,468
 (mock sobbing)

1473
00:46:39,468 --> 00:46:40,301
Please.

1474
00:46:40,301 --> 00:46:41,234
 (cyberphone beeping)

1475
00:46:41,234 --> 00:46:42,068
- Welcome back.

1476
00:46:42,068 --> 00:46:42,934
Is that the show, then?

1477
00:46:42,934 --> 00:46:43,768
 - [Tom] Oh.

1478
00:46:43,768 --> 00:46:45,034
 Heh.

1479
00:46:45,034 --> 00:46:47,034
 - [Rat Fink] Neon, I
 want to let you know

1480
00:46:47,034 --> 00:46:49,034
 that I'm completely disgusted

1481
00:46:49,034 --> 00:46:51,268
 with the work of all
 of you over there.

1482
00:46:51,268 --> 00:46:52,368
 - [Mike] I think he
 speaks for all of us.

1483
00:46:52,368 --> 00:46:53,601
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

1484
00:46:53,601 --> 00:46:54,834
  - [Rat Fink] The
  escape of the girl

1485
00:46:54,834 --> 00:46:56,401
  has all but ruined
  my last chance.

1486
00:46:56,401 --> 00:47:00,501
 We leave now with very little
 time to form a new plan.

1487
00:47:00,501 --> 00:47:02,401
- I'm sorry about what happened.

1488
00:47:02,401 --> 00:47:04,901
- [Tom] Yeah, well, sorry
don't pay the gas bill, doctor.

1489
00:47:04,901 --> 00:47:06,001
 - Around now.

1490
00:47:07,268 --> 00:47:09,934
 How is it coming at the cave?

1491
00:47:09,934 --> 00:47:12,634
How are all my monsters?

1492
00:47:12,634 --> 00:47:14,634
- Never mind about the monsters.

1493
00:47:14,634 --> 00:47:17,201
 Keep your thinking on
 what has to be done.

1494
00:47:17,201 --> 00:47:18,734
 It's going to be more
 difficult than ever

1495
00:47:18,734 --> 00:47:21,034
  now because I have learned
  through the grapevine

1496
00:47:21,034 --> 00:47:25,201
 that Batwoman herself is
 guarding the vault at Ayjax,

1497
00:47:25,201 --> 00:47:26,901
  taking no chances
  of our formulating

1498
00:47:26,901 --> 00:47:29,168
a successful operation.

1499
00:47:29,168 --> 00:47:30,901
But we'll do it anyway.

1500
00:47:30,901 --> 00:47:33,434
 Success will be ours.

1501
00:47:33,434 --> 00:47:35,334
 Do you understand me, Neon?

1502
00:47:35,334 --> 00:47:36,668
  - Oh, could you
  start again, right

1503
00:47:36,668 --> 00:47:39,901
 after the part where
 you were reaming me?

1504
00:47:39,901 --> 00:47:42,668
 Well, the ball's in
 our court, Heathcliff.

1505
00:47:42,668 --> 00:47:43,901
  (thunder crashing)

1506
00:47:43,901 --> 00:47:47,301
 - [Mike] It was a
 dark and stormy, oh.

1507
00:47:47,301 --> 00:47:49,901
 - What's Dwight
 Eisenhower doing here?

1508
00:47:49,901 --> 00:47:52,634
- [Tom] Security
guards of foreign wars.

1509
00:47:52,634 --> 00:47:53,701
  (humming)

1510
00:47:53,701 --> 00:47:56,101
 - [Mike] The last brownshirt.

1511
00:47:57,434 --> 00:48:00,234
 - Where was I on the
 night of April 14th?

1512
00:48:00,234 --> 00:48:01,834
  (chuckles)

1513
00:48:01,834 --> 00:48:03,001
 I love my job.

1514
00:48:04,401 --> 00:48:06,001
 - [Tom] Oojay?

1515
00:48:06,001 --> 00:48:06,834
 Oojay?

